## 1. REAL-WORLD PROBLEMS THIS SYSTEM MUST SOLVE

Design features around these genuine pain points of railway traffic control (especially single-line and high-density Indian-style sections). Each problem maps to a feature in Section 6.

| # | Real problem railway controllers face | What RailSmart must do |
|---|---|---|
| P1 | Section controllers decide crossings and overtakes manually using control charts, phone calls and experience | Automatic crossing/overtake/precedence recommendations with reasons |
| P2 | Single-line sections: two opposite trains need a loop line to cross; wrong decisions cause long holds | Loop-line-aware CP-SAT model with crossing and meeting-point decisions |
| P3 | Freight vs passenger priority conflicts; freight gets starved or blocks express trains | Configurable priority and fairness (max freight starvation time) |
| P4 | Delay propagation (one late train delays 10 others downstream) | Delay-propagation graph and "blast radius" analysis |
| P5 | Late rake / locomotive / crew arrival (linked rakes, crew duty-hour limits) | Rake-linkage, loco and crew-duty constraints and warnings |
| P6 | Fog, heavy rain and heat cause speed restrictions and cancellations | Weather-driven speed factors, fog protocol, rule-based and ML impact |
| P7 | Temporary Speed Restrictions (TSR) and maintenance blocks (traffic and power blocks) | TSR and block planner, auto re-optimization around blocks |
| P8 | Platform shortage and platform clashes at junction stations | Platform allocation with train length, dwell and conflict avoidance |
| P9 | Passenger connections missed because a feeder train is late | Connection-protection logic (hold vs release trade-off) |
| P10 | Inaccurate ETAs shown to passengers | ML ETA with prediction intervals and confidence |
| P11 | Operators distrust black-box AI | Explainability: every recommendation shows reason, rule, delay saved and who loses time |
| P12 | Emergency, VIP and special trains must be inserted at short notice | Emergency insertion with minimal disturbance to others (re-plan in seconds) |
| P13 | Data lives in silos (spreadsheets, charts, logs) | CSV and Excel import and export plus REST API |
| P14 | No way to test "what if" before acting | What-if engine plus digital twin replay |
| P15 | Maintenance is reactive; track faults cause sudden failures | Anomaly detection on simulated sensors and maintenance planner |
| P16 | Energy waste from stop-start running | Coasting and speed-profile recommendation and energy estimate |
| P17 | Language barrier and low digital literacy among staff | Simple UI, big colour-coded alerts, English and Hindi labels toggle |
| P18 | Post-incident review is hard | Audit log, decision history and replay |

